# A flat deck with two merchants standing in it, and nothing else at all.
#
# NOT A LEVEL AND NOT MEANT TO BE PLAYED. It exists so the merchant tests measure
# on a fixture with nothing else moving in it: a dash that lands on a shopkeeper
# is the only event here, so a hat that goes missing went to the trade and not to
# a rusher. The 2026-08-14 sweep that blamed the ramps for a skirmisher's work is
# the reason this file is empty rather than borrowing playtest_bridge.
#
# TWO OF THEM, FAR APART, because "one sale per merchant" is a claim about one
# merchant and not about the species. The second is here so a test can show that
# spending the first leaves the other still open -- with one, "spent" and "the
# feature is off" produce identical readings.
#
# The clear rows in front of each are dash runway: a dash covers 5.6 m and the
# cell is 2 m, so an approach needs three cells of nothing to be a dash rather
# than a walk that happens to arrive.

name = test_merchant
base_height = 0
width = 30
length = 12
tags = foot, test

